  "query_preview": ".. /Tuesday through Saturday/... A low pressure system \nand associated front looks to bring rain area wide and stronger \nwinds to Dixon Entrance to Clarence Strait (up to 20 kts). That \ninitial system looks to weaken Wednesday, before it interacts with\nanother system near Prince William Sound and once again increases\nrain chances Friday. \n\nBased on the location of these systems, they look to bring the \nheaviest rainfall totals and highest wind speeds to the Southern \nPanhandle. The weather pattern overall is looking fairly wet for the \nend of July. While the Northern Panhandle looks to be a bit drier, \nsome Northern inland location could have high temperatures in the \n70s.",
